From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:13:20 -0500
Subject: feat: a folder's minus closes its open pins and collapses it

A folder in the pinned run, a nested one included, shows a minus at the end of
its header while the pointer is on that header and the folder holds an open
pin of the Space on screen. It is the rows' close button on their column, and
it takes its room from the name only while it shows, so nothing else on the
row moves. It does not show in the rail, during a rename or Change Icon, while
the header is dragged or while a tab is dragged over it. A folder under the
Clear line has none: its tabs are plain rows, and Close Folder's Tabs is the
command that deletes rows (folders F44).

A press does to each open pin what Cmd-W does, through the same path
(SleepOrLeaveToClose): the pin sleeps at home and stays a pin, a page that can
ask "Leave site?" asks first, and the window lands where Cmd-W lands. Once no
page has kept its pin the folder collapses with nothing left out, whatever is
selected and whatever "Keep open tabs out of a collapsed folder" says
(SpaceModel::CollapseFolderLeavingNothingOut). Stay leaves the folder open. With
"Cmd-W on a pinned tab puts it to sleep" off the press closes the open pins by
Close Folder's Tabs' own close, which now takes a list (folders F45).

Close Open Tabs and Collapse on the header's menu does the same, for the
keyboard and in the rail (folders F46; menus M7).

Why: the reporter's second ask on GitHub issue 78 and the owner's yes of
2026-11-05, shown on hover (BACKLOG S-425).

Removable when: never as behaviour.
